      "query": "{\"content\": \"Distributed for its first conference following a requested response; expect the Court to deny the petition without further relists. The petition presents a question regarding prejudgment interest on noneconomic damages under Section 1983. However, the circuit split appears shallow, relying heavily on dicta and cross-statute analogies rather than a direct conflict on Section 1983 itself. Furthermore, the presence of waiver/forfeiture issues regarding the statute-specific arguments be",
